{"id":"src/lib/nl2sql/pipeline.ts","pkg":"src/lib/nl2sql","kind":"module","lines":272,"commentLines":27,"header":["The flow is: question -> (LLM writes SQL) -> guard -> read-only execution -> answer. If the guard rejects the SQL or the database fails on it, I show the model the exact problem and give it up to two more attempts. Everything external (the model, the database) is injected, so I can test the whole flow without either."],"symbols":[{"name":"confirmedExamples","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":30,"sig":"const confirmedExamples = ttlMemo(() => PERF.nl2sqlExamplesCacheSeconds, (c: SqlClient) => loadConfirmedExamples(c))","type":"","doc":["Here I pass the context for a second attempt after a \"No\", and other optional inputs. I read the two lists of example queries from the log table (200 rows each) on every question, so I remember them for a short while instead (src/lib/perf/switches.js: nl2sqlExamplesCacheSeconds; 0 = read every time)"],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"1f62b35c27-confirmedExamples","usedBy":[]},{"name":"negativeExamples","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":31,"sig":"const negativeExamples = ttlMemo(() => PERF.nl2sqlExamplesCacheSeconds, (c: SqlClient) => loadNegativeExamples(c))","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"1f62b35c27-negativeExamples","usedBy":[]},{"name":"PipelineExtra","kind":"interface","exported":true,"line":33,"generics":"","extends":"","doc":[],"members":[{"kind":"field","name":"retryOf","line":35,"type":"number | null","optional":true,"readonly":false,"doc":["The log row of the answer that was rejected; I store it on the new row as retry_of."]},{"kind":"field","name":"rejectedSql","line":37,"type":"string[]","optional":true,"readonly":false,"doc":["SQL the model must not produce again: the rejected answer."]},{"kind":"field","name":"hint","line":39,"type":"string","optional":true,"readonly":false,"doc":["The person's reason, turned into an instruction for the model (see learning.ts retryHint)."]}],"id":